erent uniforms than  mitsuri despite mitsuri supposedly  having the standard for female slayers  apparently maida masao a perverted  uniform sewer for the demon slayer core  makes them specifically to be  open-chested however upon seeing that  shinobu poured oil onto her uniform and  threw matches on it in front of maida  telling kano and ali to do the same  murad the most recurring background  demon slayer was in the same final  selection as sabito and giu he was also  apparently given a compliment from a  girl he liked about his hair and since  then has put extra effort into making it  look perfect hotaru the sword smith for  the demon slayer core is typically seen  in a hyotoko mask usually described as  having a puckered face and often  different sized eyes  while there are different stories for  this in different regions of japan in  iwate where i lived for a year the myth  was that there was a boy with an odd  face who had the ability to make gold  from his belly button if someone died he  would show up at their house with a  hyotoko mask and put it on their  fireplace this in hopes of bringing  their family good fortune going forward  much like hotaro orokodaki also wears a  mask this is because he has a very  gentle face and demons would make fun of  him otherwise his mask is based on a  tengu a mythological yokai which were  sometimes considered to be shinto gods  most relevantly in the story of minamoto  yoshitsune a young boy named ushiwaka  maru is taught swordsmanship by atengu  to get revenge against a clan that  killed his father which is pretty  similar to orokodaki training tanjiro to  avenge his family and protect nezuko  jigiro was the only hashira to not have  his title based purely on his breathing  style while he was the thunder hashira  and he did use thunder breathing he was  typically referred to as the roaring  hashira which instead refers to the  sound that thunder makes and when you  consider that sound breathing comes from  thunder breathing it's a pretty cool  link kane might have been one of the  strongest hashira in the series while  others are definitely powerful in their  own right we often see the higher  echelon of the upper moons being taken  down by multiple demon slayers akkasa  doma and kokushibo are each individually  miles beyond what the hashira have to  offer however kane was able to battle  with upper moon 2 doma until sunrise on  equal footing while she ultimately would  die from her injuries it still says  quite a bit about her that she could  hold her own against doma for so long  especially when you consider that  rengoku who was considered extremely  powerful among the hashira was barely  able to keep up with upper moon 3 for a  night  shinjuro rengoku is a character that a  lot of people have issues with he's just  kind of a jerk all around and while we  do see a softer side from him in  specific scenes especially when we look  at him actually coming to terms with his  dead wife or dead son it's hard to deny  that he's one of the most hateable  characters in the series and this is  only pushed further when we learn in the  first handbook that he hates animals so  much that he wouldn't let kyojiro get a  pet because of course this character  hates animals you may have noticed that  the rengoku family has a very  distinctive hairstyle and apparently  this is caused by an ancestor who ate  too much tempura i'm not sure how this  dyed their hair but it looks pretty cool  so maybe i'll give it a go kyojiro's  mother ruka has very unusual eyes during  pregnancy in the rengoku family the  women traditionally stare into flames  for hours on end this in hopes that it  will inspire their child to grow  stronger ruka apparently did this so  much that it actually dyed her eyes  crimson giyutomioka has a spinoff which  is fittingly called giyutomioka  the amount of wisteria within shnobu's  body has been retconned by gotoge  originally being said to have 70 times  the lethal amount for a d