s the  fastest developing hashira each becoming  a hashida only two months after picking  up a sword for the first time which is  insane when you consider that tanjiro  trained with rokodaki for two years  tengen and jigoro are the only known  hashira to retire due to disability  rather than age or death  interestingly jigoro was a thunder  breathing user while tengen is a sound  breathing user which of course derives  from thunder breathing each hashira has  a specific region that they have to  protect  the leader of the demon slayers kageyau  ubuyashiki inherited his position at the  age of 4 after his father took his own  life at 19. furthermore all of the other  male siblings that he had died in suit  this all pushes into the fact that the  entire family had been cursed for  birthing the original demon muzon over a  thousand years ago this interestingly  ties muzon and the demon slayer core  together very very intimately regardless  every man in the ubu yashiki family  would meet their death before the age of  30 while every woman would have to be  married off or change their names when  they become 13 otherwise they will also  be killed or die  at that point  it's definitely an interesting curse to  deal with in a series that reflects the  series antagonist who fears mortality  pretty directly  in contrast to the ubu yoshiki family  muzon is effectively immortal outside of  being caught in sunlight his primary  goal is to achieve the ability to walk  under the sun and truly become immortal  and overcome the fear and trauma that he  dealt with having been a very weak and  sick human to overcome the sun muzon has  to find the blue spider lily a flower  which rarely blooms and even then only  blooms during the day this altogether  makes his quest kind of a fool's errand  yushiro and chachamaru are likely the  only demons left alive at the end of the  main demon slayer story demon slayer  pays homage to several other manga and  anime series but one of the earliest 